  "findings": [
    "1.6.1 (#500) builds `HistGradientBoostingRegressor(max_iter, learning_rate, max_depth, validation_fraction=0.1, n_iter_no_change=10, random_state=42)`; the v2 `gradientBoosting` predictor passes max_depth, learning_rate and max_iter only. For fewer than 10000 training pairs sklearn does not early-stop and the two are identical (`small`). With more pairs early stopping is on and v2 draws its validation split from the global numpy stream instead of random_state=42: B5 must add `random_state=42`, `validation_fraction=0.1` and `n_iter_no_change=10` (the last two equal sklearn's defaults).",
    "Default hyperparameters: 1.6.1 first grid point max_iter=100, learning_rate=0.1, max_depth=5 (grid max_depth 5/10/30); v2 declares max_iter=100, learning_rate=0.1, max_depth=6 (space 3..12). Only max_depth differs.",
    "1.6.1 selects the `landmark_genes` list while loading the CSVs (hyperparameter `gene_list`, a missing gene raises); the v2 preset consumes the whole gene expression view (`scaledGeneExpression` without `gene_list`). The case compares a pre-selected matrix; wiring the list into the preset belongs to B5.",
    "Features agree to float32 precision (class forward): v2 holds them as float32, 1.6.1 as float64. HistGradientBoosting bins the features itself in float64, and the bin boundaries agree."
  ],
